    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_fruits_nuts_vegetables; wd_term=coconut; wd_relation=skos:relatedMatch): 26 of 34 rows are counted by Number (25 in the Annual Statements 1856–66, from the British West Indies and British Guiana; one CUST 4 row in 1840), i.e. coconuts; the cocoa-bean anchor was wrong. Layer-1 observations: 34 rows, 1800–1866. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×25; KEW_CUST 4 ×6; KEW_CUST 5 ×3. Units: Number ×26; CWTS (Hundredweights) ×3; Hundredweights.Quarters.Pounds ×3; Lbs. (Pounds) ×2. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×4; Canada → England ×4; Other Parts → United Kingdom ×3; British West India Islands → United Kingdom ×3."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0843" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cocoa nuts"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_25470>, <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300262559>, <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3342808>, <http://zbw.eu/stw/descriptor/14066-0> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Period-dependent heading: in 1856–66 Annual Statements 'Cocoa nuts' are coconuts (entered by number, from the West Indies and Guiana); of the 9 earlier CUST 4/5 rows (1800–1840), 8 are entered by weight and may be cacao, which early ledgers also called 'cocoa nuts'; the ninth (1840) is entered by number."@en ;
